  <figcaption>Dominant block, THE MARGINS: both pre-registered decision strata, cs.CL and cs.CV,
  one row each, their four margin metrics against the fitted ordinary-drift envelope and one-sided
  prediction band (2015H1&#8211;2022H2 fit, extrapolated through 2026H1) &mdash; the collapse-side
  bound is never crossed by a sustained (two-consecutive) run in any of the eight. The control
  stratum math.NT is not drawn in this block. Smaller, secondary block, THE FINGERPRINT (labelled
  non-decisional on the figure itself): the same dossier's declared post-2022 marker-word pool
  rate, read for all three strata on one axis &mdash; not a margin metric and not part of the §7
  verdict above it. Every figure is read at runtime from the frozen
  <code>results/results.json</code>; method and full numbers in <code>./README.md</code>.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>What the margins say</h3>
      <p>Lexical diversity (MTLD), hapax share, the Zipf-tail slope and inter-abstract
      similarity are each fit an ordinary-drift envelope on 2015H1&#8211;2022H2 and checked,
      one-sided, in their own collapse direction through 2026H1. No metric sustains a
      collapse-side breach: the kill condition in the pre-registration fires, and the
      verdict for cs.CL and cs.CV alike is <strong>NO SIGNAL BEYOND ORDINARY DRIFT</strong>.
      Where MTLD leaves the band, it leaves it on the <em>anti</em>-collapse side &mdash;
      texts got more lexically diverse, not less &mdash; which the one-sided test was never
      built to flag as a finding either way.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>What the fingerprint says</h3>
      <p>The marker channel is not a margin metric and carries no collapse direction of its
      own; it is watched in the excess direction only. Its pool rate climbs sharply from
      2023 in both cs.CL and cs.CV &mdash; the two strata where model-assisted writing is
      expected &mdash; and stays flat in the math.NT control. The fingerprint of new usage
      arrived. The margins it was expected to shrink did not.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="objection">
    <h3>What this does and does not claim</h3>
    <p>This instrument does <strong>not</strong> claim the four margin metrics are the only
    way homogenization could show up, nor that a null result on this pre-registered design
    rules out change by other measures. It claims exactly what the pre-registration
    committed to check, checked the same way in both directions: on this design, over this
    corpus and window, the previously reported margin decline does not continue, plateau, or
    reverse detectably beyond ordinary drift &mdash; while the declared marker vocabulary's
    rise is exactly where a model-assisted-writing account would put it, and absent from the
    control. Full arithmetic, the pre-registration text, and every number drawn above:
    <code>./README.md</code> and <code>./SOURCES.md</code>.</p>
  </div>

